# will_follow_one_ending — following somebody has one ending, the place AND the hour together
#
# A stalk passes the hour and moves the body. The planner read those as two separate ends, and one
# was a place the follower never stands: still where they began, at the later hour. At this forge in
# the afternoon the only trader there sells no real weapon, and another apprentice who does comes back
# for the evening, so Armoury Lore planned "follow her, then meet him" in two steps, though following
# her ends in the Back Lane, away from the forge he trades at. Its real way is to find him where he
# stands now and be led back: three steps.
#
# Pinned to a generated village, because the case needs a trader's schedule and a catalogue, which the
# test location does not roll. If this scene is rebuilt differently, find another by reading
# `inspect will` at each hour, rather than loosening the assertions.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed -2106049018 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --npc-affinity CloseFriend --location-type village --location-id 24900 --start-area "Forge" --period afternoon --grant-mm armoury_lore --organs all=5

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

advance 12 180
expect-state will "will armoury_lore steps=3 first="
expect-no-state will "will armoury_lore steps=2"
quit
